# Terminal descriptions rihla installs into ~/.terminfo when the system has none
# (CentOS/RHEL 7 lacks both; macOS lacks tmux-256color):
#
#   tmux-256color  what programs inside rihla's tmux see as $TERM (italics, true key
#                  codes); without it tmux would fall back to screen-256color.
#   xterm-kitty    what kitty sends over SSH; without it tmux refuses to start
#                  ("missing or unsuitable terminal: xterm-kitty") and less/nano complain.
#
# Both are copied from ncurses' terminfo.src (ncurses snapshot, 2026; "kitty" there is
# named xterm-kitty here, which is the name kitty sets) and flattened with
# `infocmp -x -1 -A`. Changes: pairs#0x7fff instead of 0x10000 so the old ncurses 5.9 of
# CentOS 7 can read the compiled files, and Tc on xterm-kitty (kitty draws 24-bit colour).
#
# The compiled files next to this one (t/tmux-256color, x/xterm-kitty) are what the
# installer copies. They were built from this file with the tic of ncurses 5.9 (CentOS 7),
# whose format every ncurses reads:   tic -x -o DIR rihla.src
#	Reconstructed via infocmp from file: ti/./t/tmux-256color
tmux-256color|tmux with 256 colors,
	OTbs,
	OTpt,
	am,
	hs,
	km,
	mir,
	msgr,
	xenl,
	AX,
